From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Bergin <peter@berginkonsult.se>
Date: Thu, 6 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix ONNX_ML not applied to Python bindings on non-MSVC

add_onnx_global_defines() propagates compile definitions such as
ONNX_ML=1 to a target. For onnx_cpp2py_export it was only called
inside if(MSVC), so on Linux/GCC/Clang the definition was never
set and the Python module was compiled without ONNX_ML even when
-DONNX_ML=1 was passed to cmake.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [fixed differently in upstream via nanobind migration]

Signed-off-by: Peter Bergin <peter@berginkonsult.se>

---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index a0e098ff..00000002 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -651,8 +651,8 @@ if(BUILD_ONNX_PYTHON)
                             )
     endif()
     add_msvc_runtime_flag(onnx_cpp2py_export)
-    add_onnx_global_defines(onnx_cpp2py_export)
   endif()
+  add_onnx_global_defines(onnx_cpp2py_export)
 endif()

 # Export include directories
--
2.34.1
